  "faithful": "BUXUS, in botany, a genus of the monœcia tetrandria class. The calix of the male consists of three leaves; and the corolla has two petals: The calix of the female has four leaves; the petals are three; it has three filaments, and the capsule has three cells containing two seeds. There is but one species, viz, the sempervirens, or box-tree, a native of Britain. A decoction",
